      "writtenOn": "2026-02-05T13:53:14Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Yes and ERR_PTR doesn\u0027t fix the problem here. Originally I brought hyp_alloc_errno() to keep it simple for the allocation\n\n```\nif (!ptr) return err;\n```\n\nJust like with kmalloc().\n\n\u003e  I am still not convinced what does it buy us to differentiate between ENOMEM and ENOMEMHYPALLOC ?\n\nSo currently ENOMEM means a lot of things and things that can ENOMEM are hyp stage-1, vcpu memcache, hyp_alloc() ... it has caused problems in the past already and in a later patch, I do bring a new one: host stage-2 (ENOMEMHOSTS2) \n\nSo the idea is to simply be able to propagate a meaningful error so the caller can know what to do.",
